## 🧠 4. The AI Council — Multi-Model Consensus

This is the brain of CYPHEX. Instead of trusting one AI, we use a **council of local LLMs** that debate, validate, and cross-check each other's work. This prevents hallucinations from breaking your code.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph SELECTOR["🎛️ Model Selector"]
        direction LR
        HW["🖥️ Hardware Detection<br/>GPU VRAM · RAM"]
        STRAT["📐 Strategy Selection<br/>Solo / Dual / Full Council"]
        HW --> STRAT
    end

    subgraph COUNCIL["🧠 AI Council (via Ollama)"]
        direction TB
        
        subgraph DEBATE["⚖️ Vulnerability Debate"]
            V1["🔎 Validator 1<br/>Confirms or rejects<br/>each finding"]
            V2["🔎 Validator 2<br/>Independent cross-check"]
            V3["🔎 Validator 3<br/>Tie-breaker vote"]
            V1 --> VOTE["🗳️ Majority Vote<br/>Confirmed / False Positive"]
            V2 --> VOTE
            V3 --> VOTE
        end

        subgraph REPORTING["📊 Analysis Council"]
            NARRATOR["✍️ Narrator Model<br/>Drafts security report<br/>OWASP · CWE · CVSS"]
            FACTCHECK["🔍 Fact-Checker Model<br/>Cross-validates claims<br/>against raw evidence"]
            NARRATOR --> FACTCHECK
        end

        subgraph PATCHING["🛠️ Patch Council"]
            PATCHER["💊 Patcher Model<br/>Writes the code fix<br/>(Best code specialist)"]
            REV1["✅ Reviewer 1<br/>Validates safety<br/>(Different model)"]
            REV2["✅ Reviewer 2<br/>Validates safety<br/>(Different model)"]
            PATCHER --> REV1
            PATCHER --> REV2
            REV1 --> CONSENSUS["🏛️ Consensus<br/>Safe / Review Needed / Rejected"]
            REV2 --> CONSENSUS
        end
    end

    STRAT --> COUNCIL
```

### Execution Strategies

The Model Selector dynamically adapts to your hardware:

| Strategy | VRAM Needed | Models Loaded | Use Case |
|:---|:---:|:---:|:---|
| 🏋️ **Solo Powerhouse** | < 8 GB | 1 large model | Limited hardware — one model does all tasks |
| ⚡ **Dual Specialist** | 8–12 GB | 2 models | Code specialist + reasoning validator |
| 🏛️ **Full Council** | 12+ GB | 3+ models | Parallel debate + cross-model consensus |

### The Patching Workflow (Step by Step)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant E as 🖥️ Engine
    participant S as 🎛️ Selector
    participant P as 💊 Patcher
    participant R1 as ✅ Reviewer 1
    participant R2 as ✅ Reviewer 2
    participant V as 🔬 Syntax Validator
    participant FS as 📂 Filesystem
    participant GH as 🐙 GitHub

    E->>S: Select best models for patching
    S-->>E: Patcher + 2 Reviewers

    loop For each vulnerability
        E->>P: Send vulnerable code + CWE
        P-->>E: Returns fixed_code JSON
        E->>R1: Review original vs. patch
        R1-->>E: Approved ✅ / Rejected ❌
        E->>R2: Review original vs. patch
        R2-->>E: Approved ✅ / Rejected ❌
        
        alt Majority Approved
            E->>V: Syntax validation (node -c / python -m py_compile)
            alt Valid Syntax
                V-->>E: ✅ Pass
                E->>FS: Write patched file
            else Invalid Syntax
                V-->>E: ❌ Fail — skip patch
            end
        else Rejected
            E-->>E: Skip — log rejection reason
        end
    end

    E->>GH: git add → git commit → git push
```

