## 🔄 7. Integration Workflows

### A. CLI Workflow (`cyphex scan`)

The primary user-facing workflow. One command triggers the entire 8-step pipeline.

```mermaid
graph LR
    CMD["⌨️ cyphex scan ./app"] --> CLONE["📥 Clone / Copy"]
    CLONE --> SAST["🔍 Static Scan<br/>Cyphex + Semgrep"]
    SAST --> SANDBOX["📦 Deploy Sandbox"]
    SANDBOX --> DAST["💥 Dynamic Scan<br/>14 Agents + Nuclei"]
    DAST --> IMMUNE["🧬 Immune System<br/>Red vs Blue"]
    IMMUNE --> REPORT["📊 Security Report<br/>AI-generated"]
    REPORT --> PATCH["🛠️ Auto-Patch<br/>Council consensus"]
    PATCH --> PUSH["🐙 Git Push<br/>Commit fixes"]
```

### B. GitHub Webhook (`cyphex webhook`)

Zero-command security — every `git push` triggers a scan automatically.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Dev as 👤 Developer
    participant GH as 🐙 GitHub
    participant Hook as 🪝 Cyphex Webhook<br/>localhost:3005
    participant Engine as ⚙️ Scan Engine
    participant PR as 📝 Pull Request

    Dev->>GH: git push
    GH->>Hook: POST /api/github/webhook
    Hook->>Engine: Clone repo → Full scan
    Engine->>Engine: SAST + DAST + Immune + Patch
    Engine->>GH: Create branch cyphex/auto-fix-*
    Engine->>PR: Open Pull Request with fixes
    PR-->>Dev: Review & merge security patches
```

### C. Live Auto-Healing (`cyphex watch`)

Real-time protection using the RASP SDK embedded in the running application.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Hacker as 🏴‍☠️ Attacker
    participant App as 🌐 App + RASP SDK
    participant Daemon as 👁️ Cyphex Daemon<br/>localhost:3004
    participant Council as 🧠 AI Council
    participant Code as 📂 Source Code

    Hacker->>App: SQL Injection attempt
    App->>App: 🛡️ RASP blocks attack (403)
    App->>App: 📸 Captures exact stack trace<br/>file:line of vulnerable code
    App->>Daemon: POST /api/telemetry/attack
    Daemon->>Council: Trigger patch generation
    Council->>Council: Model 1 drafts fix
    Council->>Council: Model 2 reviews safety
    Council->>Code: Write verified patch to disk
    Note over Code: Auto-healed while app stays online
```

