## 🔐 9. Security Principles

| Principle | Icon | How CYPHEX Implements It |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| **Offline-First** | 🔒 | All AI models run locally via Ollama. Zero source code leaves the machine. |
| **Multi-Model Consensus** | 🏛️ | No single AI can apply a patch. Majority vote required from independent models. |
| **Syntax Guardrail** | 🚧 | Every AI-generated patch is compiled (`node -c` / `python -m py_compile`) before being written. |
| **Sandboxed Testing** | 📦 | All dynamic attacks run inside isolated Docker or subprocess sandboxes. |
| **Genetic WAF** | 🧬 | No hardcoded regex rules. The immune system evolves detection mathematically. |
| **RASP Stack Traces** | 📍 | Live runtime protection gives EXACT file:line of vulnerable code, not URL guessing. |

